# Changelog fragments are append-only, so take both sides of every merge.
#
# Five merges in one day produced the same corruption: two branches append a
# fragment at the same offset, the `[[fragments]]` header line is identical
# context on both sides, and the three-way merge keeps one header for two ids.
# The second id then parses as a duplicate key inside the first fragment, the
# file stops being valid TOML, and every release-docs verdict behind the parse
# becomes unreachable until someone recognizes the failure. Union merge keeps
# both sides' added lines, headers included, which is the correct resolution for
# a file nobody edits in place.
release/changes/unreleased.toml merge=union
